r renders the lazy canvas branch — canvas chunks and all CAD URLs stay unfetched. Mid-session toggle: canvas unmounts; drei's GLTF cache retains parsed data and past requests can't be revoked — the GLM report states this honestly.\n- Two doc comments (StationNav, BootSequence) match the new behavior; no narrative/ladder edits, no CAD touched.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\n`runtime/lifecycle/posters-policy-parent/report.json` (parent run, 23:47–23:51Z): V4 pass — reduced-motion-static desktop+narrow: `requests: []`, `glbRequests: []`, probe `status: \"ready\"`; poster cases additionally show `glCanvasCount: 0`, `threeScene: null`. Source tests 445/43 and build 703 PASS per spec.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe earlier canvas-observables caveat is now closed by direct measurement: the parent opening roster's reduced cases (`runtime/opening-posters-policy-parent/desktop-reduced.json` and `narrow-reduced.json`) both record `passed: true`, `errors: []`, `failures: []`, `cadRequests: []`, `canvases: []` at before/settled/scrolled/returned, harness GL contexts with `connected: false` and zero draws, the reduced-motion poster line \"REDUCED MOTION PREFERRED; ANIMATED 3D DISABLED\" present, DOM station nav present, and Lenis absent — direct proof of no CAD requests and no connected WebGL canvas for fresh reduced startup, desktop and narrow. Scoped reduced-policy browser acceptance now passes on direct observables. V6 is a parent/manual review-protocol gate, not an executable browser assertion: report.json always records it null/pending as metadata, while gates/runtime.md closes it from the actual parent rerun plus independent reviews — the JSON null is a recording limitation, not an open gate. The full opening roster remains active and desktop full already failed at 110 s after stepping to lite; that failure is outside this change's scope — no full-roster acceptance is claimed and no cause is diagnosed here. This is a GLM review; it cannot claim a Fable verdict.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"s